<bx:output>
<h1>Error catalog</h1>
<p>Each link throws an uncaught error: ColdBox answers with a 500 (or the status shown) through <code>main.onException</code>.
Add <code>?caught=1</code> to catch it in the handler instead and get a normal page.</p>
<table>
	<tr><th>Kind</th><th>What it does</th><th>Uncaught</th><th>Caught</th></tr>
	<bx:loop array="#prc.kinds#" item="k">
		<tr>
			<td><code>#k.action#</code></td><td>#encodeForHTML( k.what )#</td>
			<td><a href="#event.buildLink( 'errors.' & k.action )#">run</a></td>
			<td><a href="#event.buildLink( linkTo = 'errors.' & k.action, queryString = 'caught=1' )#">run</a></td>
		</tr>
	</bx:loop>
</table>
<p><a href="/cbApp/public/index.bxm/nosuchhandler/index">A URL that matches no handler</a> goes to <code>main.notFound</code> (404).</p>
</bx:output>
